# Railway soft-launch deployment

## Project pin

- **Project:** `iotfabrikken-softlaunch`
- **Service:** `web` (must track GitHub repo `vb-iotfabrikken/Webpage`)
- **Branch:** `soft-launch` only — **never** `master`
- **URL:** https://web-production-52760.up.railway.app

Railway deploys from the Dockerfile (`railway.json` → `DOCKERFILE`). The Dockerfile
rejects non-`soft-launch` Railway builds and forces `LAUNCH_LIVE_ONLY = true` at
build time regardless of branch source file.

## Branch workflow

| Branch | `LAUNCH_LIVE_ONLY` in source | Purpose |
|--------|------------------------------|---------|
| `master` | `false` | Full-site local dev |
| `soft-launch` | `true` | Railway production soft launch |

Feed `soft-launch` from `master` deliberately (cherry-pick or targeted merge), not
by auto-syncing whole `master`.

## How to deploy

### Normal workflow

1. Commit and push to `origin/soft-launch` — GitHub webhook auto-deploys.

### Recovery (if the branch pin drifts or deploys show `master` commits)

1. Reconnect the source branch:
   `railway service source connect --repo vb-iotfabrikken/Webpage --branch soft-launch --service web`
2. Confirm in the Railway dashboard: **web** → Settings → Source → branch =
   `soft-launch`.
3. Push to `origin/soft-launch` to trigger a fresh deploy.

To redeploy an existing good build without rebuilding from git, use **Redeploy** on
that deployment in the dashboard (redeploys the same commit/image).

## CLI and dashboard pitfalls (learned 2026-06-30)

Do **not** use these for soft-launch deploys — they pull `master` even when the
dashboard is pinned to `soft-launch`:

- **`railway redeploy --from-source`**
- **Dashboard "Deploy Latest Commit"** (command palette) — uses the GitHub default
  branch (`master`)

Also avoid:

- **`railway up`** — fails with 413 Payload Too Large (~1.2 GB) because the repo
  archive is too big for CLI upload. Use GitHub-triggered deploys instead.

## Trust center during soft launch

- Security pillar slug: `platform/security` (links to Platform hub on full launch).
- During soft launch, `platform/security` is in `SOFT_LAUNCH_HIDDEN_TRUST_PILLARS`
  — the card is removed entirely (same as Terms and SLA).
- Only **Privacy & GDPR** (`legal/privacy`) shows as a linked pillar.
